cate contacts. Shared notes and session state keep everyone in sync — all in real-time.What this means: Run a multi-op contest station with Propulse as your coordination hub.Live ConnectionDisconnectedTest ConnectionArchitectureThe bridge sits between your browser and hardware, routing messages over localhost.Propulse(Browser)Bridge Serverlocalhost:9867WebSocketHamlibrigctldDX ClusterTelnetWSJT-XUDP 2237Your RadioTransceiverMessage ProtocolAll messages use a JSON envelope format with type, id, timestamp, and payload fields.Security ModelBinds exclusively to localhost (127.0.0.1) — no remote connections acceptedCAT control commands cannot be issued from outside your computerContest data and QSO information never leave your local networkNeed remote access for multi-computer setups?ssh -L 9867:127.0.0.1:9867 user@contest-pcSSH tunnels forward the bridge port securely. Only use this with trusted machines and authenticated SSH keys.Setup GuidePick your platformSteps shown for macOS.WindowsmacOSLinux1Install the BridgeClone or download the Propulse repository, then install dependencies:cd bridge
